# Meridian Interface — environment configuration
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values. `.env.local` is gitignored.
#
# NOTE: Any variable prefixed with VITE_ is inlined into the client bundle at build
# time and is therefore PUBLIC (readable by anyone who views the site). Never put a
# real secret (API keys, private tokens, database passwords) behind a VITE_ prefix.
# Secrets belong on the server side — see the marketing-stack backend integration.

# --- Lead / booking submission endpoint (backend integration) ---
# Bookings + inquiries POST here (in addition to being stored locally).
# Defaults to the Meridian marketing-system intake webhook when left blank, so
# the site captures leads out of the box. Override only to point at a different
# backend. The intake webhook is a PUBLIC endpoint — no secret is exposed here.
VITE_LEAD_ENDPOINT=""

# --- Owner portal soft gate ---
# Passcode for the internal owner invoice portal. This is a *soft* client-side gate
# only (see note above — it is not real authentication). Real access control must be
# enforced server-side once the backend is connected. If unset, a build-time default
# is used for local development.
VITE_OWNER_PASSCODE=""
